From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ming Lei <ming.lei@clyso.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 06:45:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] os/bluestore/BlueFS: fix envelope header alignment for non-4K
 page hosts

The envelope-header assert in append_try_flush() requires the memory
address of a new header to mirror its file position modulo
CEPH_PAGE_SIZE. CEPH_PAGE_SIZE is the host VM page size resolved at
runtime, but the write path only keeps the two positions congruent at
the smaller of the page size and the BlueFS block size: envelope
flushes pad the on-disk stream to super.block_size, while fresh
appender chunks are page-aligned allocations.

On hosts whose page size exceeds the BlueFS block size (16K Apple
Silicon, 64K aarch64 kernels) a block-aligned WAL position is usually
not page-aligned, so the assert fires on ordinary RocksDB WAL writes
and every OSD aborts at startup. Direct I/O only requires block-size
memory alignment (see KernelDevice's
rebuild_aligned_size_and_memory), so assert the congruence the code
actually maintains: modulo min(CEPH_PAGE_SIZE, super.block_size).

Also round up instead of truncating in the FileWriter appender sizing:
with bluefs_alloc_size at or below the page size (e.g. 4K alloc on a
16K-page host) min_pages integer-truncated to 0, making refill()
allocate nothing so append_hole() fell back to an unaligned buffer -
the assert would then fire even at block-size granularity.

Introduced by 4c03bbea4437 ("os/bluestore/bluefs: Add assert if write
buffer is not page aligned"); first released in v20.2.3.

Fixes: https://tracker.ceph.com/issues/79141
Signed-off-by: Ming Lei <ming.lei@clyso.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0479d49eff70d09ccde516c029929f5d39a29c27)
---
 src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.cc | 7 ++++++-
 src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.h  | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.cc b/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.cc
index d3c4b752434..13cab0638be 100644
--- a/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.cc
+++ b/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.cc
@@ -4085,7 +4085,12 @@ void BlueFS::append_try_flush(FileWriter *h, const char* buf, size_t len)/*_WF_L
       h->envelope_head_filler = h->append_hole(File::envelope_t::head_size());
       uint32_t pos1 = h->get_effective_write_pos() - File::envelope_t::head_size();
       uint32_t pos2 = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(h->envelope_head_filler.c_str());
-      ceph_assert(p2aligned(pos1 ^ pos2, CEPH_PAGE_SIZE));
+      // Buffer memory must mirror the on-disk position, but only up to
+      // the smaller of the page size (alignment of fresh appender
+      // chunks) and the block size (padding granularity of envelope
+      // flushes) - the two can differ in either direction.
+      ceph_assert(p2aligned(pos1 ^ pos2,
+                            std::min<uint32_t>(CEPH_PAGE_SIZE, super.block_size)));
     }
     size_t max_size = 1ull << 30; // cap to 1GB
     while (len > 0) {
diff --git a/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.h b/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.h
index 9db3f3fec41..22a39dde111 100644
--- a/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.h
+++ b/src/os/bluestore/BlueFS.h
@@ -423,7 +423,12 @@ public:
     FileWriter(FileRef f, unsigned super_block_size)
       : file(std::move(f))
       , buffer_appender(buffer.get_page_aligned_appender(
-        std::max<uint64_t>(g_conf()->bluefs_alloc_size, 2 * super_block_size) / CEPH_PAGE_SIZE))
+        // round up: when CEPH_PAGE_SIZE exceeds the wanted capacity this
+        // must not truncate to 0 pages, or refill() allocates nothing and
+        // append_hole() falls back to an unaligned buffer
+        p2roundup<uint64_t>(
+          std::max<uint64_t>(g_conf()->bluefs_alloc_size, 2 * super_block_size),
+          CEPH_PAGE_SIZE) / CEPH_PAGE_SIZE))
       , envelope_head_filler() {
       ++file->num_writers;
       iocv.fill(nullptr);
